From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alejandro Garcia <skipper.pelygro@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 18:05:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: gs201-panther: give the fuel
 gauge its battery model

Give the gauge the ModelGauge m5 model that the stock kernel loads for
the pack with a 1 kOhm ID resistor (Coslight, cos-a1-1k in Google's
gs201-panther-battery-data.dtsi), as the Pixel 7 Pro does with its own.
The phone's pack is that one: under stock's driver the gauge's TempCo
read 0x1a02, this model's, where the 0 and 3 kOhm models have 0x223e and
0x1802. RelaxCfg takes the value stock writes over the model at boot
(r_regval_1720x in the live device tree); the rest, FilterCfg included,
is Google's, and the same as the live tree's.

On a POR, the driver writes the model into the gauge's RAM and clears
POR. With it, the gauge measures the battery thermistor, and one
capacity LSB becomes 2 mAh (TaskPeriod 0x2d00).

Tested on a Pixel 7 from slot B (7.3.0-rc6), on top of the previous
patch, with the gauge in POR: the driver logs "battery model loaded
(DesignCap 0x873, TaskPeriod 0x2d00)". On the cable it then read 92 %
(99 % with the default model), 4.33 V, 33.1 C (22.0 C before),
charge_full 4324 mAh of 4326 mAh design, and Charging. upower and the
shell show 92 %. With the cable out for a minute, btop showed a
discharge of 1.38-1.67 W from it. No I2C errors. The gauge's interrupt
fired in bursts, about 1300 times while the model loaded and about 400
during the unplug, and was quiet otherwise.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Alejandro Garcia <skipper.pelygro@gmail.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-panther.dts  | 51 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 47 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-panther.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-panther.dts
index a3008a7da..cae0e762a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-panther.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-panther.dts
@@ -199,10 +199,6 @@ &hsi2c_13 {
 	clock-frequency = <400000>;
 	status = "okay";
 
-	/*
-	 * No battery model yet: the gauge reports from its default one, so
-	 * the capacity and the temperature are approximate.
-	 */
 	fuel-gauge@36 {
 		compatible = "maxim,max77759-fg";
 		reg = <0x36>;
@@ -212,6 +208,53 @@ fuel-gauge@36 {
 		/* maxim,rsense-default = <500> (10 uOhm units) in the live tree */
 		shunt-resistor-micro-ohms = <5000>;
 		monitored-battery = <&battery>;
+
+		/*
+		 * Battery model for the pack with a 1 kOhm ID resistor, the one
+		 * this phone has (the gauge's TempCo read 0x1a02 under stock's
+		 * driver, which is this model's). From Google's
+		 * gs201-panther-battery-data.dtsi (cos-a1-1k, model version 2),
+		 * except RelaxCfg 0x143b, the value stock writes over the
+		 * model's at boot (r_regval_1720x). TaskPeriod 0x2d00 makes one
+		 * capacity LSB 2 mAh with 5 mOhm: DesignCap 0x0873 = 4326 mAh.
+		 */
+		maxim,fg-model = /bits/ 16 <
+			0x8c80 0xb770 0xb8f0 0xba50 0xbb40 0xbc30 0xbe00 0xbfd0
+			0xc1b0 0xc3a0 0xc6b0 0xc9c0 0xd020 0xd300 0xd5e0 0xdc30
+			0x0080 0x1070 0x1020 0x0ed0 0x0f00 0x1700 0x1530 0x0c20
+			0x0c40 0x07f0 0x07f0 0x06f0 0x0710 0x06d0 0x06f0 0x06f0
+			0x0200 0x0200 0x0200 0x0200 0x0200 0x0200 0x0200 0x0200
+			0x0200 0x0200 0x0200 0x0200 0x0200 0x0200 0x0200 0x0200
+		>;
+		maxim,fg-params = /bits/ 16 <
+			0xf060	/* IAvgEmpty */
+			0x143b	/* RelaxCfg */
+			0x260e	/* LearnCfg */
+			0x4217	/* Config: external thermistor, TEx clear */
+			0x0090	/* Config2 */
+			0x5f00	/* FullSOCThr */
+			0x0873	/* FullCapRep */
+			0x0873	/* DesignCap */
+			0x3200	/* dPAcc */
+			0x021c	/* dQAcc */
+			0x0873	/* FullCapNom */
+			0xa561	/* VEmpty */
+			0x1f00	/* QRTable00 */
+			0x0d80	/* QRTable10 */
+			0x0480	/* QRTable20 */
+			0x0400	/* QRTable30 */
+			0x0740	/* RComp0 */
+			0x1a02	/* TempCo */
+			0x0557	/* IChgTerm */
+			0xed51	/* TGain */
+			0x1eba	/* TOff */
+			0x0014	/* Curve */
+			0x3870	/* MiscCfg */
+			0x1900	/* AtRate */
+			0x2241	/* ConvgCfg */
+			0xc613	/* FilterCfg */
+			0x2d00	/* TaskPeriod */
+		>;
 	};
 };
 
